cff-version: 1.2.0
title: MicroSUS.jl
message: >-
  If you use this software in academic work, please cite it
  using the metadata in this file, and cite the DATASUS
  microdata you analysed as a separate data source.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Dante
    family-names: Bertuzzi
    email: dantesbertuzzi@gmail.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/dantebertuzzi/MicroSUS.jl'
url: 'https://dantebertuzzi.github.io/MicroSUS.jl/'
abstract: >-
  Julia package for reading Brazilian public health
  microdata (DATASUS): constant-memory streaming reads of
  .dbc (PKWare DCL) and .dbf files, per-system typed schemas
  (SIM, SINASC, SIH, SIA, CNES, SINAN), CP850 to UTF-8
  transcoding, cached downloads with provenance records,
  resumable downloads and mirrors, a data manifest that pins
  the exact files an analysis read, and a Tables.jl interface
  with partitions; plus IBGE population denominators (by age
  and sex, and by health region), embedded municipality and
  ICD-10 tables, data quality audits and the RIPSA mortality
  indicators (infant, maternal, ill-defined causes, premature
  NCD mortality).
keywords:
  - julia
  - datasus
  - public-health
  - epidemiology
  - microdata
  - brazil
  - dbc
license: MIT
version: 0.5.0
date-released: 2026-10-04
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22164178
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22164178
    description: >-
      Concept DOI — always resolves to the most recent
      version of MicroSUS.jl. Each release also gets its own
      DOI, minted by Zenodo after the release is published
      (so it cannot be recorded in the release itself); see
      the Zenodo page for the DOI of every version.
